  "report_period": "Week 35 (21st Aug to 28th Aug 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Mount Dampier\" 181/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 11/2026, Scrubber fitted) was committed to European interests at xs USD 38 mill. Please note that earlier this month, the sister vessel \"Orange Tiger\" 181/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS 11/2030, DD 09/2028) was sold at USD 36,5 mill and the one-year-older \"Cape Condor\" 180/2010 Koyo, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 04/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold at USD 39 mill. Mykonos Shipping have committed the Kamsarmax \"Efraim A\" 82/2010 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 05/2030, DD 05/2028) to undisclosed interests at USD 20 mill. By way of comparison, the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Polynesia Queen\" 82/2012 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 05/2027) was sold in July at USD 21 mill. The Ultramax \"Amaryllis\" 63/2013 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 08/2028) of NG Livanos Maritime was committed to Chinese interests at low-mid USD 24 mill. Remind you that a couple of months ago, the \"Ultra Saka\" 63/2013 Chengxi, China (SS 06/2028, DD 09/2026) was sold at USD 23,2 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"African Wagtail\" 58/2013 DACKS, China (SS 10/2028, DD 10/2026) was committed at xs USD 20 mill, while the sister vessel \"African Tern\" 58/2013 DACKS, China (SS/DD 06/2028) was sold in June at high USD 19 mill. Moreover, Byzantine Maritime committed their \"Marianna\" 55/2010 IHI, Japan (SS 03/2030, DD 03/2028) at USD 17 mill. By way of comparison, the \"Capt Eugene\" 55/2010 Mitsui, Japan (SS 06/2030, DD 09/2028) was sold a month ago at USD 16,8 mill. In addition, following the sale of the \"Spar Libra\" 53/2006 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 04/2026) back in February at USD 9 mill, clients of Spar Shipping have now committed the sister vessel \"Spar Scorpio\" 53/2006 Chengxi, China (SS/DD 10/2026) to Chinese interests at low-mid USD 11 mill. Arklow Shipping have committed their Handysize \"Arklow Spirit\" 36/2013 Dae Sun, Korea (SS 12/2028, DD 10/2026) to undisclosed interests at USD 16,6 mill. For reference, the \"DL Olive\" 35/2013 Spp, Korea (SS 12/2028, DD 11/2026) was sold in March at USD 15,3 mill.",
    "tankers": "The Aframax \"Seasenator\" 105/2007 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS/DD 01/2027) of Valles Steamship was committed to undisclosed interests at high USD 30's mill. For reference, the \"Volta River\" 105/2007 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS/DD 08/2027) was sold in early March at rgn USD 33 mill. Flyte Logistics have committed their MR2 \"Mumbai\" 46/2003 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 10/2028, DD 10/2026) at USD 10,4 mill. Note that the one-year- older \"Lanikai\" & \"Caroline\" 46/2002 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 12/2027 &SS/DD 11/2027) were sold a couple of months ago at USD 9,5 mill each.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route maintained an active presence, with Port Hedland and Dampier departures to Qingdao settling between USD 14.15/15.30 fio. In the Atlantic, Tubarao fixtures to Qingdao, including West Africa options, achieved between USD 37.25/37.50 fio. Out of South Africa, a Saldanha Bay run to Qingdao fetched USD 26.14 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with Singapore-Japan options settled between USD 18,500/20,500 pd. Australian rounds with redelivery in South China and Singapore-Japan ranges fetched between USD 16,000/21,500 pd. Indonesian coal runs to South China, India and regional destinations achieved between USD 12,100/17,500 pd, while a South East Asia trip via South Africa to Singapore-Japan made USD 20,250 pd. From East Coast India, East Africa and regional origins, trips via ECSA to Far East destinations obtained between USD 16,500/25,000 pd, alongside an ECSA departure securing USD 21,000 pd plus USD 1,000,000 ballast bonus. In the Atlantic, transatlantic and fronthaul fixtures via USEC and US Gulf range ranged from USD 26,100 to USD 32,750 pd. On period, activity was brisk with vessels securing between USD 17,500/22,250 pd for durations ranging from 5 to 14 months.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, a North China trip via NoPac to Australia settled at USD 19,000 pd, while a South China run to WCSA made USD 19,000 pd. Indonesian coal trips with options to India, China and regional destinations achieved between USD 15,000/23,000 pd, whereas steel, slag and clinker runs from North China to East Coast India range secured between USD 18,500/23,000 pd. Out of West Coast India, trips to East Coast India and Singapore-Japan range obtained USD 24,000 pd and USD 16,600 pd respectively. In the Atlantic, transatlantic grain and coal fixtures from US Gulf to Continent and East Med reached between USD 27,000/32,000 pd, while a petcoke run to South East Asia made USD 31,000 pd. Out of Continent, trips to East Med and East Africa settled between USD 21,000/21,500 pd. On period, vessels secured between USD 19,000/22,750 pd for durations ranging from 5 to 13 months.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Pacific, Indonesian clinker runs to South China and Taiwan settled at USD 15,000 pd, while a South East Asia trip via Australia to Singapore-Japan range also fetched USD 15,000 pd. A South China trip with Singapore-Japan options for 2 to 3 laden legs made USD 15,800 pd. In the Atlantic, Continent trips via Murmansk and Baltic options to Continent and West Africa ranges obtained between USD 15,850/17,000 pd, while a prompt Continent run to West Africa fixed at USD 16,500 pd. Out of South America, a West Coast South America coastal trip secured USD 16,750 pd."
    }
  },
